  "term": "in-house evaluation",
  "definition": "In-house evaluation is an assessment of a method using a clinical dataset gathered within the same research or clinical setting that developed it, rather than only testing transfer to a public or external dataset. In the source, it refers to supervised testing of the segmentation framework on an in-house thyroid ultrasound dataset.",
